                        "entry_id": "b81fcc36-a6e8-399c-a141-9b0d45ab6822",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The vital principle or force believed by the Paracelsians to be responsible for alchemical reactions within living bodies, and hence for the growth and continuation of life."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1ee4cee3-ae2d-4d53-b6f9-c5d09376436e",
                                "sense_id": "8602aca7-4e33-3707-81cb-9f1af52878c9",
                                "text": "[…] it must be the Modus of some other Substance latitant in the fluid Matter, and really distinguishable from it; which is either the Soul, or some seminal Form or Archeus, as the Chymist calls it […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cab44015-d721-40ce-9cf5-655e61457657",
                                "sense_id": "8602aca7-4e33-3707-81cb-9f1af52878c9",
                                "text": "Willis rejected not just scholasticism's ‘substantial forms’ but Paracelsus's ‘archeus’ doctrine as well."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7c720094-5ab0-4410-a684-f4d762a8148f",
                                "sense_id": "8602aca7-4e33-3707-81cb-9f1af52878c9",
                                "text": "But Paracelsus' theory of the archeus and the alchemy of life inevitably led him into deeper waters."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
